    <p class="profile-summary" id="summary"><em>Murasaki Shikibu (c. 973 – c. 1014 or 1025) was a lady-in-waiting at the Heian court who, from a learned Fujiwara household, wrote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-tale-of-genji">The Tale of Genji</a>, a diary and a collection of poems. Her husband died after about two years of marriage, and scholars still disagree about when she died.</em></p>

